{"task_id": "Mbpp/63", "solution": "from typing import List, Tuple, Union\ndef max_difference(tuple_list: List[Tuple[Union[int, float], Union[int, float]]]) -> Union[int, float]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the maximum absolute difference between available pairs in the given tuple list.\n\n    Args:\n        tuple_list: A list of tuples, where each tuple contains exactly two numerical elements\n                    (integers or floats).\n\n    Returns:\n        The maximum absolute difference found. Returns 0 if the input list is empty.\n\n    Raises:\n        TypeError: If the input 'tuple_list' is not a list.\n        ValueError: If any element in the 'tuple_list' is not a tuple of exactly two numbers,\n                    or if the elements within a pair are not numerical.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(tuple_list, list):\n        raise TypeError(\"Input 'tuple_list' must be a list.\")\n\n    if not tuple_list:\n        return 0\n\n    differences = []\n    for pair in tuple_list:\n        if not isinstance(pair, tuple) or len(pair) != 2:\n            raise ValueError(\"Each element in the list must be a tuple of exactly two numbers.\")\n        if not all(isinstance(x, (int, float)) for x in pair):\n            raise ValueError(\"Both elements in a pair must be numerical (int or float).\")\n        differences.append(abs(pair[0] - pair[1]))\n\n    return max(differences)"}
