{"task_id": "Mbpp/82", "solution": "import math\ndef volume_sphere(radius):\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the volume of a sphere.\n\n    Args:\n        radius (float or int): The radius of the sphere.\n\n    Returns:\n        float: The calculated volume of the sphere.\n\n    Raises:\n        TypeError: If radius is not a numeric value.\n        ValueError: If radius is negative.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(radius, (int, float)):\n        raise TypeError(\"Radius must be a numeric value.\")\n    if radius < 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"Radius cannot be negative.\")\n        \n    return (4/3) * math.pi * (radius ** 3)"}
