{"task_id": "Mbpp/84", "solution": "class NewmanConwaySequenceCalculator:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates terms of the Newman-Conway sequence using memoization.\n    P(1)=1, P(2)=1, P(n) = P(P(n-1)) + P(n-P(n-1)) for n > 2.\n    \"\"\"\n    def __init__(self):\n        self._memo = {1: 1, 2: 1}\n\n    def _calculate_term(self, n: int) -> int:\n        \"\"\"\n        Internal recursive method to calculate P(n) with memoization.\n        Assumes n is a positive integer.\n        \"\"\"\n        if n in self._memo:\n            return self._memo[n]\n\n        # P(n) = P(P(n-1)) + P(n-P(n-1))\n        p_n_minus_1 = self._calculate_term(n - 1)\n        term1 = self._calculate_term(p_n_minus_1)\n        term2 = self._calculate_term(n - p_n_minus_1)\n\n        result = term1 + term2\n        self._memo[n] = result\n        return result\n_calculator_instance = NewmanConwaySequenceCalculator()\ndef sequence(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Returns the nth number in the Newman-Conway sequence.\n\n    Args:\n        n: The positive integer index of the desired term.\n\n    Returns:\n        The nth Newman-Conway number.\n\n    Raises:\n        ValueError: If n is not a positive integer.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(n, int) or n <= 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"Input 'n' must be a positive integer.\")\n\n    return _calculator_instance._calculate_term(n)"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/84", "solution": "def sequence(n):\n    \"\"\"\n    Computes the nth Newman-Conway number using memoization.\n    \"\"\"\n    memo = {}\n\n    def _sequence_recursive(k):\n        \"\"\"\n        Helper function to recursively calculate Newman-Conway numbers with caching.\n        \"\"\"\n        if k in memo:\n            return memo[k]\n\n        if k <= 2:\n            result = 1\n        else:\n            # P(n) = P(P(n-1)) + P(n-P(n-1))\n            p_n_minus_1 = _sequence_recursive(k - 1)\n            p_p_n_minus_1 = _sequence_recursive(p_n_minus_1)\n            p_n_minus_p_n_minus_1 = _sequence_recursive(k - p_n_minus_1)\n            result = p_p_n_minus_1 + p_n_minus_p_n_minus_1\n\n        memo[k] = result\n        return result\n\n    return _sequence_recursive(n)"}
