{"task_id": "Mbpp/96", "solution": "import math\ndef divisor(number: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the number of positive divisors for a given integer.\n    The input is assumed to be a positive integer.\n    \"\"\"\n    count = 0\n    # Iterate from 1 up to the square root of the number\n    for i in range(1, int(math.sqrt(number)) + 1):\n        if number % i == 0:\n            # Add 2 to count for i and number/i\n            count += 2\n            # If i*i is equal to number, it means i and number/i are the same\n            # In this case, we've double-counted, so subtract 1\n            if i * i == number:\n                count -= 1\n    return count"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/96", "solution": "def divisor(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the count of positive divisors for the input integer n.\n    Assumes n is a positive integer based on critical requirements.\n    \"\"\"\n    count = 0\n    for i in range(1, n + 1):\n        if n % i == 0:\n            count += 1\n    return count"}
