{"task_id": "Mbpp/101", "solution": "class InvalidInputError(Exception):\n    \"\"\"Custom exception for invalid input to kth_element function.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, message: str):\n        super().__init__(message)\n        self.message = message\ndef kth_element(array: list[int], k: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the kth element in the given array using 1-based indexing.\n\n    Args:\n        array: The list of integers.\n        k: The 1-based index of the element to find.\n\n    Returns:\n        The element at the kth position (1-based) in the original array.\n\n    Raises:\n        InvalidInputError: If the array is empty, k is non-positive,\n                           or k is greater than the array's length.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not array:\n        raise InvalidInputError(\"Input array cannot be empty.\")\n    if not isinstance(k, int) or k <= 0:\n        raise InvalidInputError(\"k must be a positive integer (1-based index).\")\n    if k > len(array):\n        raise InvalidInputError(f\"k ({k}) is out of bounds for array of length {len(array)}.\")\n\n    return array[k - 1]"}
