{"task_id": "Mbpp/103", "solution": "import math\ndef eulerian_num(n, m):\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the Eulerian number A(n, m) for non-negative integers n and m.\n    It counts permutations of {1, ..., n} with m ascents.\n\n    Args:\n        n: The first non-negative integer.\n        m: The second non-negative integer (0 <= m < n, or n=0, m=0).\n\n    Returns:\n        The integer value of A(n, m).\n\n    Raises:\n        TypeError: If n or m are not integers.\n        ValueError: If n or m are negative.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(n, int) or not isinstance(m, int):\n        raise TypeError(\"Inputs n and m must be integers.\")\n    if n < 0 or m < 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"Inputs n and m must be non-negative.\")\n\n    # Special case A(0, 0) = 1 as per definition.\n    if n == 0 and m == 0:\n        return 1\n    \n    # As per definition, A(n, m) = 0 if m is out of range [0, n-1].\n    if m >= n:\n        return 0\n\n    result = 0\n    for k in range(m + 1):\n        term = ((-1)**k) * math.comb(n + 1, k) * ((m + 1 - k)**n)\n        result += term\n    return result"}
