{"task_id": "Mbpp/109", "solution": "def odd_Equivalent(binary_string: str, rotations: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Counts how many decimal equivalents of rotated binary strings are odd.\n    Assumes valid binary string and non-negative rotations as inputs.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not binary_string:\n        return 0\n\n    odd_count = 0\n    current_binary_string = binary_string\n\n    for _ in range(rotations):\n        # A binary number is odd if its least significant bit (rightmost digit) is '1'.\n        if current_binary_string[-1] == '1':\n            odd_count += 1\n        # Perform a single left rotation on the string.\n        current_binary_string = current_binary_string[1:] + current_binary_string[0]\n        \n    return odd_count"}
