{"task_id": "Mbpp/109", "solution": "def odd_equivalent(binary_string: str, num_rotations: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the number of odd decimal equivalents after num_rotations of the binary_string.\"\"\"\n\n    def _rotate_string_inline(s: str) -> str:\n        \"\"\"Performs a single left rotation on the input string.\"\"\"\n        if not s:\n            return s\n        return s[1:] + s[0]\n\n    string_length = len(binary_string)\n    if num_rotations == 0:\n        return 0\n\n    odd_status_first_cycle = []\n    current_binary_string = binary_string\n\n    # Determine odd/even status for each unique rotation in one full cycle.\n    for _ in range(string_length):\n        decimal_value = int(current_binary_string, 2)\n        odd_status_first_cycle.append(decimal_value % 2 != 0)\n        current_binary_string = _rotate_string_inline(current_binary_string)\n\n    total_odd_count = 0\n    odd_count_in_cycle = sum(odd_status_first_cycle)\n\n    # Calculate count for full cycles of rotations.\n    full_cycles = num_rotations // string_length\n    total_odd_count += full_cycles * odd_count_in_cycle\n\n    # Calculate count for any remaining rotations in the current cycle.\n    remaining_rotations = num_rotations % string_length\n    for i in range(remaining_rotations):\n        if odd_status_first_cycle[i]:\n            total_odd_count += 1\n            \n    return total_odd_count"}
