{"task_id": "Mbpp/126", "solution": "def sum(num1: int, num2: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the sum of common divisors between two positive integers.\n    Assumes inputs are valid positive integers.\n    \"\"\"\n    divisors1 = set()\n    # Calculate all positive divisors for the first number\n    for i in range(1, int(num1**0.5) + 1):\n        if num1 % i == 0:\n            divisors1.add(i)\n            divisors1.add(num1 // i)\n\n    divisors2 = set()\n    # Calculate all positive divisors for the second number\n    for i in range(1, int(num2**0.5) + 1):\n        if num2 % i == 0:\n            divisors2.add(i)\n            divisors2.add(num2 // i)\n\n    # Find the common divisors by intersecting the two sets\n    common_divs = divisors1.intersection(divisors2)\n    \n    # Sum the common divisors using the built-in sum function\n    return __builtins__.sum(common_divs)"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/126", "solution": "import builtins\ndef sum(num1: int, num2: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the sum of common divisors for two given positive integers.\n    This function trusts the caller's inputs and performs no validation.\n    \"\"\"\n    divisors1 = set()\n    # Finds all positive divisors for the first number up to its square root.\n    for i in range(1, int(num1**0.5) + 1):\n        if num1 % i == 0:\n            divisors1.add(i)\n            divisors1.add(num1 // i)\n\n    divisors2 = set()\n    # Finds all positive divisors for the second number up to its square root.\n    for i in range(1, int(num2**0.5) + 1):\n        if num2 % i == 0:\n            divisors2.add(i)\n            divisors2.add(num2 // i)\n\n    # Identifies common divisors and computes their total sum.\n    common_divisors = divisors1.intersection(divisors2)\n    return builtins.sum(common_divisors)"}
