{"task_id": "Mbpp/140", "solution": "from typing import Iterable, Set, Union\ndef extract_singly(list_of_iterables: list[Iterable[Union[int, float]]]) -> Set[Union[int, float]]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Flattens a list of iterables (e.g., tuples, lists) into a single set of unique numbers.\n\n    Args:\n        list_of_iterables: A list where each element is an iterable containing numbers.\n                           Example: [(3, 4, 5), (4, 5, 7), (1, 4)]\n\n    Returns:\n        A set containing all unique numbers from the input iterables.\n        Example: set([3, 4, 5, 7, 1])\n    \"\"\"\n    unique_numbers = set()\n    for inner_iterable in list_of_iterables:\n        if not isinstance(inner_iterable, Iterable):\n            # Skip non-iterable elements in the top-level list for robustness\n            continue\n\n        for item in inner_iterable:\n            if isinstance(item, (int, float)):\n                unique_numbers.add(item)\n    return unique_numbers"}
