{"task_id": "Mbpp/141", "solution": "def pancake_sort(arr: list) -> list:\n    \"\"\"Sorts the input list using the pancake sort algorithm.\n    It returns a new sorted list, leaving the original unchanged.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(arr, list):\n        raise TypeError(\"Input must be a list.\")\n\n    n = len(arr)\n    if n <= 1:\n        return list(arr)\n\n    # Create a mutable copy to perform in-place sorting\n    mutable_arr = list(arr)\n\n    def _find_max_index(current_arr: list, current_n: int) -> int:\n        \"\"\"Finds the index of the maximum element within the first current_n elements of current_arr.\"\"\"\n        max_val = current_arr[0]\n        max_idx = 0\n        for i in range(1, current_n):\n            if current_arr[i] > max_val:\n                max_val = current_arr[i]\n                max_idx = i\n        return max_idx\n\n    def _flip(current_arr: list, k: int) -> None:\n        \"\"\"Reverses the order of the first k elements in the list current_arr in-place.\"\"\"\n        start = 0\n        end = k - 1\n        while start < end:\n            current_arr[start], current_arr[end] = current_arr[end], current_arr[start]\n            start += 1\n            end -= 1\n\n    for curr_size in range(n, 1, -1):\n        # Find index of the maximum element in mutable_arr[0...curr_size-1]\n        max_idx = _find_max_index(mutable_arr, curr_size)\n\n        # If max element is not already at its correct position\n        if max_idx != curr_size - 1:\n            # Move the maximum element to the beginning\n            _flip(mutable_arr, max_idx + 1)\n\n            # Move the maximum element to its correct position\n            _flip(mutable_arr, curr_size)\n    \n    return mutable_arr"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/145", "solution": "def max_Abs_Diff(arr: list[int | float]) -> int | float:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the maximum absolute difference between any two elements in an array.\n    Returns 0 if the array has fewer than two elements.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not arr or len(arr) < 2:\n        return 0\n    \n    min_val = arr[0]\n    max_val = arr[0]\n\n    for x in arr:\n        if x < min_val:\n            min_val = x\n        if x > max_val:\n            max_val = x\n            \n    return max_val - min_val"}
