{"task_id": "Mbpp/160", "solution": "def _extended_gcd(a: int, b: int) -> tuple[int, int, int]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Implements the Extended Euclidean Algorithm.\n    Returns (gcd(a, b), x, y) such that ax + by = gcd(a, b).\n    \"\"\"\n    if a == 0:\n        return (b, 0, 1) # Base case for the recursive algorithm.\n    \n    gcd_val, x1, y1 = _extended_gcd(b % a, a)\n    x = y1 - (b // a) * x1\n    y = x1\n    return (gcd_val, x, y)\ndef find_solution(a: int, b: int, n: int) -> tuple[int, int] | None:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds integer solutions (x, y) for the equation ax + by = n.\n    Returns (x, y) as a tuple if a solution exists, otherwise None.\n    \"\"\"\n    # Handle the special case where both coefficients are zero.\n    if a == 0 and b == 0:\n        return (0, 0) if n == 0 else None\n\n    gcd_val, x_particular, y_particular = _extended_gcd(a, b)\n\n    # A solution exists if and only if n is divisible by gcd(a, b).\n    if n % gcd_val != 0:\n        return None\n\n    # Scale the particular solution to satisfy ax + by = n.\n    factor = n // gcd_val\n    x = x_particular * factor\n    y = y_particular * factor\n\n    return (x, y)"}
