{"task_id": "Mbpp/239", "solution": "def get_total_number_of_sequences(m: int, n: int) -> int:\n    # dp[i][j] stores the number of sequences of length i ending with value j.\n    # The table size is (n+1) x (m+1) for 1-based indexing.\n    dp = [[0] * (m + 1) for _ in range(n + 1)]\n\n    # Base case: For sequences of length 1, any value from 1 to m is valid.\n    for j in range(1, m + 1):\n        dp[1][j] = 1\n\n    # Fill the DP table for sequence lengths from 2 up to n.\n    for i in range(2, n + 1):\n        for j in range(1, m + 1):  # Iterate through possible current element values.\n            # Sum up counts from previous elements k, where j >= 2 * k.\n            # This means k can be any positive integer up to j // 2.\n            for k in range(1, j // 2 + 1):\n                dp[i][j] += dp[i - 1][k]\n\n    # The total count of valid sequences is the sum of all sequences of length n.\n    total_sequences = sum(dp[n])\n    return total_sequences"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/239", "solution": "def get_total_number_of_sequences(m, n):\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the number of sequences of length n, where each element is a positive integer,\n    greater than or equal to twice the previous element, and less than or equal to m.\n    \"\"\"\n    _memo = {}\n\n    def _dp_solve_inner(current_val, length_left, max_m):\n        \"\"\"\n        Recursive helper using dynamic programming to count sequences.\n        Counts sequences starting with `current_val` and needing `length_left` more elements.\n        \"\"\"\n        if length_left == 0:\n            return 1\n\n        if (current_val, length_left) in _memo:\n            return _memo[(current_val, length_left)]\n\n        count = 0\n        next_min_val = 2 * current_val\n        for next_val in range(next_min_val, max_m + 1):\n            count += _dp_solve_inner(next_val, length_left - 1, max_m)\n\n        _memo[(current_val, length_left)] = count\n        return count\n\n    total_count = 0\n    for start_val in range(1, m + 1):\n        total_count += _dp_solve_inner(start_val, n - 1, m)\n    return total_count"}
