{"task_id": "Mbpp/311", "solution": "def set_left_most_unset_bit(number: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Sets the leftmost unset bit in a non-negative integer.\n    Assumes the input is a valid non-negative integer as per critical requirements.\n    \"\"\"\n    if number == 0:\n        return 1\n\n    msb_pos = number.bit_length() - 1\n    for i in range(msb_pos, -1, -1):\n        if not (number >> i) & 1:  # Check if the i-th bit is 0\n            return number | (1 << i)\n\n    # If all bits up to msb_pos are set, set the next bit to the left\n    return number | (1 << (msb_pos + 1))"}
