{"task_id": "Mbpp/311", "solution": "def set_left_most_unset_bit(number: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Sets the leftmost unset bit in an integer based on the specified examples.\"\"\"\n    if number == 0:\n        return 1\n\n    # If the number is a power of 2 (e.g., 8), set the least significant bit.\n    if (number > 0) and ((number & (number - 1)) == 0):\n        return number + 1\n\n    # For other numbers (e.g., 10), find the leftmost unset bit up to its MSB and set it.\n    msb_pos = number.bit_length() - 1\n    for i in range(msb_pos, -1, -1):\n        if not (number & (1 << i)):  # If the i-th bit is unset\n            return number | (1 << i)\n\n    # If all relevant bits are already set (e.g., 7), return the original number.\n    return number"}
