{"task_id": "Mbpp/389", "solution": "def find_lucas(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the n'th Lucas number using an iterative approach.\n    It follows the definition L(0)=2, L(1)=1, and L(n)=L(n-1)+L(n-2) for n > 1.\n    \"\"\"\n    if n < 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"Input 'n' must be a non-negative integer.\")\n    if n == 0:\n        return 2\n    if n == 1:\n        return 1\n\n    a, b = 2, 1  # L(0), L(1)\n    for _ in range(2, n + 1):\n        a, b = b, a + b\n    return b"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/389", "solution": "def find_lucas(n: int) -> int:\n    if n == 0:\n        return 2\n    elif n == 1:\n        return 1\n    else:\n        a, b = 2, 1\n        for _ in range(2, n + 1):\n            a, b = b, a + b\n        return b"}
