{"task_id": "Mbpp/428", "solution": "def shell_sort(arr: list) -> list:\n    \"\"\"Sorts a list of comparable elements using the Shell Sort algorithm.\n    This function returns a new sorted list, leaving the original array unchanged.\"\"\"\n    n = len(arr)\n    if n <= 1:\n        return list(arr)\n\n    # Create a mutable copy to perform in-place sort on the copy.\n    sorted_arr = list(arr)\n\n    # Start with a large gap, then reduce the gap.\n    gap = n // 2\n    while gap > 0:\n        for i in range(gap, n):\n            temp = sorted_arr[i]\n            j = i\n            # Perform insertion sort for elements at 'gap' distance.\n            while j >= gap and sorted_arr[j - gap] > temp:\n                sorted_arr[j] = sorted_arr[j - gap]\n                j -= gap\n            sorted_arr[j] = temp\n        gap //= 2\n    return sorted_arr"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/429", "solution": "def and_tuples(tuple1: tuple[int, ...], tuple2: tuple[int, ...]) -> tuple[int, ...]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Performs an element-wise bitwise AND operation on two input tuples.\n    Returns a new tuple with the bitwise AND of corresponding elements.\n    \"\"\"\n    result = []\n    for i in range(len(tuple1)):\n        result.append(tuple1[i] & tuple2[i])\n    return tuple(result)"}
