{"task_id": "Mbpp/453", "solution": "import math\ndef sumofFactors(number: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the sum of all even factors for a given positive integer.\n    This function trusts the caller to provide valid positive integer input.\n    \"\"\"\n    # Optimization: if the number is odd, it cannot have any even factors.\n    if number % 2 != 0:\n        return 0\n\n    total_sum = 0\n    # Iterate up to the square root of the number to find factors efficiently.\n    for i in range(1, int(math.sqrt(number)) + 1):\n        if number % i == 0:\n            # Check if 'i' is an even factor and add it to the sum.\n            if i % 2 == 0:\n                total_sum += i\n\n            # Calculate the corresponding factor 'j'.\n            j = number // i\n            # Avoid double-counting when 'i' is the square root of 'number'.\n            if j != i:\n                # Check if 'j' is an even factor and add it to the sum.\n                if j % 2 == 0:\n                    total_sum += j\n    return total_sum"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/453", "solution": "def sumofFactors(number: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the sum of all even factors of a given positive integer.\"\"\"\n    total_even_factors = 0\n    for i in range(1, number + 1):\n        if number % i == 0 and i % 2 == 0:\n            total_even_factors += i\n    return total_even_factors"}
