{"task_id": "Mbpp/564", "solution": "def count_Pairs(data_list, length):\n    \"\"\"\n    Counts unordered pairs of unequal elements within a list of integers.\n    This function efficiently calculates pairs using frequency counts.\n    \"\"\"\n    if length < 2:\n        return 0\n\n    # Manually count frequencies of each number\n    frequencies = {}\n    for item in data_list:\n        frequencies[item] = frequencies.get(item, 0) + 1\n    \n    total_pairs = 0\n    unique_elements = list(frequencies.keys())\n    \n    # Iterate through unique elements to form pairs\n    for i in range(len(unique_elements)):\n        num1 = unique_elements[i]\n        count1 = frequencies[num1]\n        for j in range(i + 1, len(unique_elements)):\n            num2 = unique_elements[j]\n            count2 = frequencies[num2]\n            total_pairs += count1 * count2\n            \n    return total_pairs"}
