{"task_id": "Mbpp/585", "solution": "def expensive_items(items, n):\n    if not isinstance(items, list):\n        raise TypeError(\"Input 'items' must be a list.\")\n    if not isinstance(n, int):\n        raise TypeError(\"Input 'n' must be an integer.\")\n    if n < 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"Input 'n' cannot be negative.\")\n\n    if not items or n == 0:\n        return []\n\n    for item in items:\n        if not isinstance(item, dict):\n            raise ValueError(\"Each item in the list must be a dictionary.\")\n        if 'name' not in item:\n            raise ValueError(\"Each item dictionary must contain a 'name' key.\")\n        if 'price' not in item:\n            raise ValueError(\"Each item dictionary must contain a 'price' key.\")\n        if not isinstance(item['price'], (int, float)):\n            raise TypeError(f\"Item '{item.get('name', 'Unknown')}' has a non-numeric price: {item['price']}.\")\n\n    sorted_items = sorted(items, key=lambda x: x['price'], reverse=True)\n    return sorted_items[:n]"}
