{"task_id": "Mbpp/589", "solution": "def _is_perfect_square(num: int) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks if a non-negative integer is a perfect square.\n    Negative numbers are not considered perfect squares.\n    \"\"\"\n    if num < 0:\n        return False\n    sqrt_num = int(num**0.5)\n    return sqrt_num * sqrt_num == num\ndef perfect_squares(start: int, end: int) -> list[int]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds all perfect squares within the inclusive range [start, end].\n    Returns an empty list if start > end, or if no perfect squares are found.\n    \"\"\"\n    if start > end:\n        return []\n\n    perfect_squares_list = []\n    actual_start = max(0, start) # Perfect squares are non-negative.\n\n    for num in range(actual_start, end + 1):\n        if _is_perfect_square(num):\n            perfect_squares_list.append(num)\n    return perfect_squares_list"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/591", "solution": "def swap_List(input_list: list) -> list:\n    \"\"\"Interchanges the first and last elements of a list, returning a new list.\n    For lists with fewer than two elements, a shallow copy is returned unchanged.\n    \"\"\"\n    list_length = len(input_list)\n\n    if list_length < 2:\n        return list(input_list)\n\n    # Create a new list to avoid modifying the original\n    new_list = list(input_list)\n    new_list[0], new_list[list_length - 1] = new_list[list_length - 1], new_list[0]\n    return new_list"}
