{"task_id": "Mbpp/592", "solution": "def binomial_coeff(n: int, k: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the binomial coefficient C(n, k) efficiently.\n    Assumes n and k are non-negative integers and 0 <= k <= n.\n    \"\"\"\n    if k == 0 or k == n:\n        return 1\n    if k > n // 2:  # Optimization: C(n, k) = C(n, n-k)\n        k = n - k\n    \n    res = 1\n    for i in range(k):\n        res = res * (n - i) // (i + 1)\n    return res\ndef sum_Of_product(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the sum of the product of consecutive binomial coefficients.\n    This sum is equivalent to C(2n, n-1).\n    Assumes n is a non-negative integer.\n    \"\"\"\n    if n == 0:\n        return 0\n    \n    return binomial_coeff(2 * n, n - 1)"}
