{"task_id": "Mbpp/620", "solution": "def largest_subset(nums: list) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the size of the largest subset where every pair is divisible.\n    It sorts unique input numbers and applies dynamic programming.\n    \"\"\"\n    # Remove duplicates and sort the list to enable dynamic programming.\n    sorted_unique_nums = sorted(list(set(nums)))\n    n = len(sorted_unique_nums)\n\n    # Initialize dp array; dp[i] stores the size of the largest divisible subset ending with sorted_unique_nums[i].\n    dp = [1] * n\n    max_size = 0  # Initialize max_size. If the list is empty, loops won't run, 0 will be returned.\n\n    # Iterate through each number to build up the DP array.\n    for i in range(n):\n        # Check previous numbers for divisibility.\n        for j in range(i):\n            a = sorted_unique_nums[i]\n            b = sorted_unique_nums[j]\n\n            # Inlining divisibility check. Critical requirements forbid error handling for zero.\n            if (a % b == 0) or (b % a == 0):\n                dp[i] = max(dp[i], dp[j] + 1)\n        # Update the overall maximum size found so far.\n        max_size = max(max_size, dp[i])\n    \n    return max_size"}
