{"task_id": "Mbpp/633", "solution": "def pair_xor_Sum(numbers, N):\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the sum of XOR of all unique pairs in the given list.\n    N is assumed to be the length of the numbers list.\n    \"\"\"\n    if N < 2:\n        return 0\n\n    total_xor_sum = 0\n    for i in range(N):\n        for j in range(i + 1, N):\n            total_xor_sum += (numbers[i] ^ numbers[j])\n    return total_xor_sum"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/635", "solution": "def heap_sort(data_list: list) -> None:\n    \"\"\"\n    Sorts a list in-place using the heap sort algorithm.\n    Modifies the input list to be sorted in ascending order.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    def _heapify(arr, n, i):\n        largest = i\n        left = 2 * i + 1\n        right = 2 * i + 2\n\n        if left < n and arr[left] > arr[largest]:\n            largest = left\n\n        if right < n and arr[right] > arr[largest]:\n            largest = right\n\n        if largest != i:\n            arr[i], arr[largest] = arr[largest], arr[i]\n            _heapify(arr, n, largest)\n\n    n = len(data_list)\n\n    # Build a max-heap from the input list.\n    for i in range(n // 2 - 1, -1, -1):\n        _heapify(data_list, n, i)\n\n    # Extract elements one by one from the heap.\n    for i in range(n - 1, 0, -1):\n        data_list[i], data_list[0] = data_list[0], data_list[i]\n        _heapify(data_list, i, 0)"}
