{"task_id": "Mbpp/743", "solution": "def rotate_right(input_list, n):\n    \"\"\"\n    Rotates a list to the right by a specified number of items.\n    The original list remains unchanged, and a new list is returned.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not input_list:\n        return []\n\n    list_length = len(input_list)\n    effective_n = n % list_length\n\n    # Split the list into two parts: tail (last effective_n elements) and head (remaining)\n    head = input_list[:list_length - effective_n]\n    tail = input_list[list_length - effective_n:]\n\n    # Concatenate tail and head to form the rotated list\n    return tail + head"}
