{"task_id": "Mbpp/757", "solution": "def count_reverse_pairs(string_list: list[str]) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Counts unique pairs of strings where one is the reverse of the other.\n    Palindromes do not form pairs with themselves.\n    \"\"\"\n    unique_strings = set(string_list)\n    pair_count = 0\n    processed_pairs = set()\n\n    for s in string_list:\n        s_rev = s[::-1]\n        # Check if the reverse exists and is distinct from the original string (per BR1 and BR2).\n        if s_rev in unique_strings and s != s_rev:\n            # Normalize the pair to avoid double-counting (e.g., (\"a\", \"b\") and (\"b\", \"a\")).\n            normalized_pair = tuple(sorted((s, s_rev)))\n            if normalized_pair not in processed_pairs:\n                pair_count += 1\n                processed_pairs.add(normalized_pair)\n    return pair_count"}
