{"task_id": "Mbpp/767", "solution": "from collections import Counter\ndef get_pairs_count(numbers: list[int], sum: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Counts the number of pairs in a list whose sum is equal to \u2018sum\u2019.\n\n    Args:\n        numbers: A list of integers.\n        sum: The integer target sum.\n\n    Returns:\n        The total count of pairs that sum up to \u2018sum\u2019.\n    \"\"\"\n    freq_map = Counter(numbers)\n    pair_count = 0\n\n    for num in numbers:\n        # Decrement frequency of current number to avoid pairing with itself\n        # from the same position and to correctly handle combinations of duplicates.\n        freq_map[num] -= 1\n\n        complement = sum - num\n\n        if complement in freq_map and freq_map[complement] > 0:\n            pair_count += freq_map[complement]\n        \n    return pair_count"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/767", "solution": "def get_pairs_count(numbers: list[int], target_sum: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Counts pairs of elements in 'numbers' summing to 'target_sum', identified by distinct indices.\n    Handles duplicate numbers by considering each instance as unique.\n    \"\"\"\n    if len(numbers) < 2:\n        return 0\n\n    count = 0\n    # Manually build a frequency map for number occurrences.\n    freq_map = {}\n    for num in numbers:\n        freq_map[num] = freq_map.get(num, 0) + 1\n\n    # Iterate through the original list to consider each number and its index implicitly.\n    for num in numbers:\n        complement = target_sum - num\n\n        if complement in freq_map:\n            if complement == num:\n                # If the complement is the number itself, count pairs with other instances.\n                count += freq_map[num] - 1\n            else:\n                # If complement is different, add its frequency to the count.\n                count += freq_map[complement]\n    \n    # Each valid pair is counted twice (e.g., (a,b) when a is processed, and (b,a) when b is processed).\n    return count // 2"}
