{"task_id": "Mbpp/780", "solution": "from typing import List, Tuple\ndef find_combinations(tuple_list: List[Tuple[int, int]]) -> List[Tuple[int, int]]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates all unique pairwise sums of distinct tuples from the input list.\n    Performs input validation to ensure the list contains only tuples of two integers.\n    Returns a sorted list of these unique summed tuples.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(tuple_list, list):\n        raise TypeError(\"Input must be a list.\")\n        \n    result_set = set()\n    n = len(tuple_list)\n\n    for i in range(n):\n        t1 = tuple_list[i]\n        if not isinstance(t1, tuple) or len(t1) != 2:\n            raise TypeError(f\"Element at index {i} must be a tuple of two integers.\")\n        if not all(isinstance(x, int) for x in t1):\n            raise ValueError(f\"Elements in tuple at index {i} must be integers.\")\n\n        for j in range(i + 1, n): # Iterate for distinct pairs (j > i)\n            t2 = tuple_list[j]\n            if not isinstance(t2, tuple) or len(t2) != 2:\n                raise TypeError(f\"Element at index {j} must be a tuple of two integers.\")\n            if not all(isinstance(x, int) for x in t2):\n                raise ValueError(f\"Elements in tuple at index {j} must be integers.\")\n\n            sum_tuple = (t1[0] + t2[0], t1[1] + t2[1])\n            result_set.add(sum_tuple)\n    \n    return sorted(list(result_set)) # Sorting for consistent output for testing"}
