{"task_id": "Mbpp/797", "solution": "def sum_in_range(l: int, r: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the sum of all odd natural numbers within the inclusive range [l, r].\n    Assumes l and r are integers, l <= r, and l >= 1.\n    \"\"\"\n    # Adjust 'l' to be the first odd number in the range [l, r]\n    first_odd = l if l % 2 != 0 else l + 1\n\n    # Adjust 'r' to be the last odd number in the range [l, r]\n    last_odd = r if r % 2 != 0 else r - 1\n\n    # If the adjusted first_odd is greater than the adjusted last_odd, there are no odd numbers\n    if first_odd > last_odd:\n        return 0\n\n    # Calculate the number of odd terms in the arithmetic progression\n    # The common difference for odd numbers is 2\n    num_terms = (last_odd - first_odd) // 2 + 1\n\n    # Calculate the sum using the arithmetic progression formula: n/2 * (first_term + last_term)\n    total_sum = (num_terms * (first_odd + last_odd)) // 2\n\n    return total_sum"}
